In article <5016@mva.cs.liv.ac.uk> ian@mva.cs.liv.ac.uk (Ian Finch) writes:
>I was wandering around with a wand of polymorph and a ring of polymorph control
>when I ran into a load of orcs. I zapped myself into a demon and started bashing
>them up a bit! Then (and this is the bit I want to know about) I got a message:
>
>       some hell-p has arrived
>
>and two demons came and helped me with the orcs. They then stayed around (like
>familiars) even when I reverted to human form.
>
>My question is why did this happen? Does it always happen? Any other useful
>info? (Okay that's three questions!)

1) It happened because you were a demon & were wielding no weapon &
     attacked something hand-to-hand.  Everytime this happens, there is
     a chance that a demon (or occasionally, demon-lord) is gated in to
     help. 
2) I don't know the exact chance of this happening (I guess I could
     check the source) -- but I had a game recently where I was a demon
     who had 15 demons & a large dog trailing me through the dungeon.
     (when you have that many, they do get in your way)
3) Sometimes it is worth getting a couple of demons & then wielding a
     weapon (so that you don't summon any more)
     
